# Phase 5: Admin Dashboard

We will build a sleek, premium, and fully responsive Admin Dashboard to manage Nutrexia's products, orders, and customers.

## Open Questions & Important Notes

> [!WARNING]
> **Hostinger Deployment Quirk:** 
> Because the Admin Dashboard requires a completely different layout (Sidebar instead of the Storefront Navbar/Footer), we must use Next.js "Route Groups" (moving the storefront files into a `(storefront)` folder). 
> As we discovered earlier, Hostinger sometimes fails to delete old files during deployments. When we deploy this, you may need to manually delete the old `src/app/page.tsx` and `src/app/layout.tsx` from your Hostinger File Manager to prevent conflicts. Are you comfortable with this?

> [!NOTE]
> **Questions for you:**
> 1. **Authentication:** Should we build the Admin Dashboard UI first and mock the data, or should we immediately integrate Supabase Authentication so you have to log in to see it?
> 2. **Initial Pages:** I plan to build a general `Overview` page and a `Products` management page first. Does that sound good?

